"""Contact-approval liveness uses the database clock (F-2, H-76; additive).

Revision series: 0050, 0051 and 0052 are committed and not edited. This revision re-issues nine guard functions
whose contact-approval liveness predicate compared ``user_contact_approvals.expires_at`` with ``now()``.
``now()`` is the start time of the surrounding transaction. A transaction that began before an approval's
expiry could therefore keep treating the approval as live after its real expiration. Each affected predicate
now uses ``clock_timestamp()``, the same authoritative database clock used by the lease and ceremony paths.

Only the approval-liveness predicates change. Each is written as ``expires_at > clock_timestamp()``, so the
boundary is unchanged: an approval is live strictly before its expiry and refused at or after it. Session,
proof, token-lifetime, approval-timestamp and reservation ``now()`` uses are not changed.

Functions (owner ``webdesk_guard_owner``; each keeps its owner, grants and SECURITY DEFINER settings, because
CREATE OR REPLACE is applied under the owner role):
fn_advance_contact_revision, fn_approve_change_with_proof, fn_approve_create_with_proof,
fn_cancel_change_with_proof, fn_issue_ceremony_activation, fn_issue_owner_reset_token, fn_issue_token,
fn_reject_create_with_proof, fn_revoke_expired_activation_tokens.

Downgrade restores the exact pre-revision text of each function (captured from the head of 0052).
"""

